\paragraph{Feature normalization} 
All vector features associated with nodes and edges are normalized by dividing them by the maximum magnitude observed in the training dataset. In contrast , the  scalar edge features \(|\Delta \vec{x}_e^t|, |\Delta \vec{v}_e^t|\) are scaled using min-max normalization to ensure consistent feature ranges across training samples .

\subsection{Single Equi-Euler GraphNet Layer}
\label{sec:model}
