When matching the APD of a data set is particularly important, the APD fitting feature
of \ourtool can be used. This feature is particularly important for the two-variable models,
which otherwise do not emphasize APD accuracy and may achieve low curve error overall while having higher error during repolarization. 
An example of a fitting to both voltage and APD data is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:hybrid_fit},
where the MMS model was fit to canine endocardial data at CLs of \qty{500}{\milli\second} and \qty{260}{\milli\second}; APDs for this case were measured using a threshold of \num{0.8} corresponding to $\text{APD}_{20}$, which facilitates demonstration of the APD fitting feature. Fitting to voltage alone results in $\text{APD}_{20}$ errors of
