\subsubsection*{Lower bound for union volume estimation}
Given the state of the art, a natural question is to ask \emph{whether the query complexity of the general union volume estimation algorithm of \cite{KarpLM89} can be further improved}.
Any such improvement would speed up several important applications, cf.~Section~\ref{sec:related work}.
On the other hand, any lower bound showing that the algorithm of \cite{KarpLM89} is optimal also implies tightness of the known streaming algorithms (up to logarithmic factors), as the streaming algorithms match the static running time bound.

