% \yanheng{We answer this question negatively in the aforementioned query model. Interestingly, the algorithm of \cite{KarpLM89} does not exploit the full power of the model because it only queries containment for sampled points and does not examine numerical coordinates, yet it achieves optimal query complexity in the model.}
% We answer this question negatively in the aforementioned query model. Interestingly, while  the algorithm of \cite{KarpLM89} does not exploit the full power of the model while achieving optimal query complexity in the model (because it only queries containment for sampled points and does not examine numerical coordinates), our lower bound holds in full generality, i.e., even for algorithms that inspect and perform computations on the coordinates of sampled points.

