\begin{abstract}
Bigraphs are a versatile modelling formalism that allows easy expression of placement and connectivity relations in a graphical format.  System evolution is user defined as a set of rewrite rules. 
This paper presents a practical, yet detailed guide to developing, executing, and reasoning about bigraph models, including recent extensions such as parameterised, instantaneous, prioritised and conditional rules, and probabilistic and stochastic rewriting. 

\end{abstract}

\keywords{Bigraphs, Graph Rewriting, Rewrite Systems}

