\section{Future Plans}
Based on our preliminary research, there are several key issues that we plan to address in the future: 
% \textbf{(1)} For bytecode analysis on newly deployed contracts, the complex bytecode contracts often result in time-consuming processing. To enhance the efficiency in detecting PM attacks, we need to design an effective strategy to prioritize key functional components in bytecode.
\textbf{(1)} For static analysis on source code, our method is limited to function-level analysis. However, DeFi contracts often involve cross-contract interaction, making it difficult for LLMs to infer semantic intent solely based on function signatures. 
We plan to recover cross-contract call graphs (xCCG) for DeFi contracts, enabling a more comprehensive analysis.
\textbf{(2)} We employ baseline LLMs to take on different roles for semantic understanding and reasoning. However, compared to fine-tuning LLMs, this approach may lack task-specific adaptability. To validate this, we plan to adopt OpenAI's fine-tuning paradigm~\cite{OpenAi} to fine-tune LLMs and test detection capability.
\textbf{(3)} Beyond price variables, we plan to generalize our analysis framework to reason about these non-price state variables, extending our method to a broader class of state manipulation attacks.
% thereby broadening the applicability of our method.
Consequently, we intend to conduct further in-depth research to explore these questions thoroughly.

