\section{Network and Accelerator Co-Optimization for Spiking Neural Networks(SNNs)}\label{sec:HT}

% When designing efficient spiking neural networks for deployment on edge/cloud devices, two key questions arise. The first question pertains to the hardware platform's ability to efficiently process sparse spiking inputs, that is: \textit{how efficiently a hardware platform can process sparse spiking input?} The second question concerns how much sparsity can be achieved while maintaining the same or a similar degree of accuracy.  
In Section~\ref{sec:HA}, we present a hardware architecture and control framework that can efficiently process a sparse spiking neural network. Our primary objective is to optimize both the network and the architecture to achieve efficient processing with minimal loss in accuracy. To this end, we propose two significant approaches. Firstly, we demonstrate that the network can be optimized for efficient processing on the fixed hardware architecture via \emph{hardware-aware training} (SpikeX-HT) while preserving its accuracy. SpikeX-HT gives rise
