We further evaluate RoboMonkey's adaptability on a new robot setup. In this section, we present the fine-tuning evaluation of RoboMonkey on the LIBERO-Long benchmark, which consists of long-horizon tasks in simulation. In our experiments, we curated a new action preference dataset using the procedure described in Section~\ref{section:synthetic} for fine-tuning the action verifier. The OpenVLA-LIBERO checkpoint used for comparison was trained via behavioral cloning on successful demonstrations. All methods were evaluated across 500 trials. Table~\ref{tab:openvla_comparison_libero90} presents the results and we observe that RoboMonkey can be effectively adapted to tasks in the LIBERO environments. We find that fine-tuning both OpenVLA and action verifier results in 6.7\% improvement in average success rate compared to simply fine-tuning OpenVLA on LIBERO-Long.

