\subsection{Channel flow with friction}
\label{ssec:channel_friction}

In this Section, we consider a steady state solution of the one-dimensional shallow water equations with constant discharge $hu = q_{0}$, varying topography and friction. Given a bathymetry profile $z_{b}(x)$, we compute the  water depth that balances the flow from the integration of the momentum equation in \eqref{eq:shw}, which reduces to the following nonlinear ODE:
%
\begin{equation}\label{eq:const_discharge}
    \rpth{\frac{q_{0}^{2}}{gh^{3}} - 1}\frac{\partial h}{\partial x} = -\frac{\partial z_{b}}{\partial x} + \frac{\gamma(q_{0},h)q_{0}}{gh}
\end{equation}
%
A reference numerical solution of the ODE is computed using the RK44 method on a very fine mesh, much finer than those used in the computations. If $\gamma \neq 0$, so that bottom friction is present, this benchmark also allows to check the correctness of the implementation of the friction terms and the ability of the IMEX method to use time steps beyond the stability limit of the explicit RK methods. We consider the same channel flow benchmark employed in \cite{rosatti:2011}, for which one assumes $L = \SI{100}{\meter}$. However, we consider the smoother depth profile:
%
\begin{equation*}
    z_{b}(x) = 4.9 + 0.001 x -
    \begin{cases}
        z_{b0}\cos^{4}\rpth{\frac{\pi\rpth{x - L/2}}{2c_{0}}}, & \text{if } -c_{0} \leq x - L/2 \leq c_{0}   \\
        0 & \text{otherwise,}
    \end{cases}
\end{equation*}
%
so as achieve the correct convergence behaviour also for higher polynomial degrees. For one dimensional subcritical flows we can impose only the value of one characteristic or physical variable at each boundary. Based on physical arguments, we impose, as customary, the discharge value at the inflow boundary and the water height $h = \SI{0}{\meter}$ at the outflow boundary. We consider five meshes with $N$ elements along the $x-$axis, where $N$ ranges from $10$ to $160 $ and we consider two different values of the Manning coefficient $n$ and of $z_{b0}$, reported in Table \ref{tab:channel_table}.

