Despite Wi-Fi's expansion into 6~GHz, achieving reliable indoor wireless coverage remains challenging due to Wi-Fi's lower power and contention-based Medium Access Control (MAC) layer. While the 4G/5G scheduled MAC is more robust, indoor coverage from outdoor macro deployments is similarly challenged due to building penetration losses. Indoor solutions such as Distributed Antenna Systems (DAS) for cellular tend to be very expensive and are not scalable.

