\begin{abstract}
After a very long winter, the Artificial Intelligence (AI) spring is here. Or, so it seems over the last three years. AI has the potential to impact many areas of human life--personal, social, health, education, professional. In this paper, we take a closer look at the potential of AI for Enterprises, where decision-making plays a crucial and repeated role across functions, tasks, and operations. We consider Agents imbued with AI as means to increase decision-productivity of enterprises. We highlight six \emph{tenets} for Agentic success in enterprises, by drawing attention to what the current, \texttt{AI-Centric~User} paradigm misses, in the face of persistent needs of and usefulness for \emph{Enterprise Decision-Making}. In underscoring a shift to \textbf{\texttt{User-Centric~AI}}, we offer six tenets and promote market mechanisms for platforms, aligning the design of AI and its delivery by Agents to the cause of enterprise users.
\end{abstract}

