Here, we write $\mu^{-i}$ as a shorthand for $\mu^{1,2,\dots,i-1,i+1,\dots,d}$. On the other hand, it is not hard to see that indeed, 
$$ \E_{i\sim d}\E_{F_1,\dots,F_{i-1},F_{i+1},\dots,F_d\sim \mu^{-i}} \Var_{\mu_{F_1,\dots,F_{i-1},F_{i+1},\dots,F_d}}(f) = \cE_{P^\vee_d}(f,f).$$
Therefore, \eqref{eq:localtoglobal1}  implies 
$$ \Var_\mu(f) \leq d\cdot \max\{i\cdot (d+1-i): i\in [d]\}\cdot  \cE_{P^\vee_d}(f,f)\Rightarrow \lambda(P^\vee_d)\geq \frac{4}{d(d+1)^2}$$

