\end{equation}
where $\beta=\frac{d}{d-1}\cdot \frac{1}{1-\alpha}$.
Now, by the conditional independence property, $\mu_{F_i}$ is a product distribution. Namely, let $\nu_1=\mu_{F_i}^{1,\dots,{i-1}}$ and $\nu_2=\mu_{F_i}^{i+1,\dots,d}.$ Then, $\mu=\nu_1\otimes\nu_2$. Therefore, by \cref{lem:varfactorization},  we have
