\section{Beyond $1/2$-Top-Link Expansion}\label{sec:scolor}
%\textcolor{red}{sh:I moved the next paragraph to intro.}
%Given an integer $k \geq 0$ and a parameter $s \geq 1$, we define the $s$-analog of $k$ and of $k!$ via
