\subsection{ADRD Classification Methods}
We conducted our ADRD-oriented method selection (Figure \ref{method_search}) by searching on Google Scholar on August 13th, 2024 for papers that cited the ADReSSo-2021 Challenge report \cite{luz2021detecting}. This resulted in 139 papers. Next, the additional search term 'github' was used to filter those papers for the ones with open-source code repositories. This resulted in 43 papers. A manual assessment was then conducted on these 43 papers to determine if they contained a link to a github repository of code written by the authors. After this manual assessment, 12 papers included repositories containing code for the methods of the paper. Four of these repositories contained complete, working code that predicted ADRD from recordings of speech and transcripts derived from CTT recordings, which were ultimately included in this study: 
