\begin{abstract}
We describe a recently revived version of the software package \SubalgberaBases, which is distributed in the \Macaulay\ computer algebra system.
The package allows the user to compute and manipulate subagebra bases ---  which are also known as SAGBI bases or canonical bases and form a special class of Khovanskii bases --- for polynomial rings and their quotients.
We provide an overview of the design and functionality of \SubalgberaBases\ and demonstrate how the package works on several motivating examples.
\end{abstract}

