\section{Conclusions} \label{sec:conc}
Starting from a pair of multiderivative Explicit and Implicit Taylor methods, it is possible to derive the fourth-order Gauss–Legendre Runge–Kutta method, along with its associated conjugate symplectic scheme.  
This derivation naturally leads to a higher-order dense output formula for the same method, which is intrinsically linked to the scheme and requires only one additional function evaluation.

An open question remains: \textit{Is it possible to extend this theory to higher-order Gauss–Legendre Runge–Kutta schemes?}




